\0
The loss of Gunawan left Freedom Guard forces in disarray, and several of their allies in the rim sectors were overcome by the Imperium. Only Perlen, Strata and a few minor worlds under Freedom Guard control remain untouched. Radec was injured in the siege of Indra and was treated at a field hospital on Elmaean while second in command, Gerhad Bantrill, and what remained of the Freedom Guard Synod attempted to regroup their forces on Elmaean. However, the Imperium followed on their heels in an attempt to deal them a death blow.
\1
We have recently received several encoded transmissions from Baator. Apparently Commanders Radec and Bantrill escaped aboard a transport ship during the destruction of Indra.  Fortunately Baator has reached such stature in Radec's command that he is considered essential to their war effort, and he was evacuated with the others to a provisional base at Elmaean. Strike now while they are regrouping.\n\n
We have placed a new weapon at your disposal. Use the Rift Creator and swiftly cleanse the universe of this cancer before it spreads again. Radec is injured and being treated in a hospital on Elmaean. If you can eliminate him, some of his forces will surely mutiny and turn on each other. Make sure he does not leave the planet alive.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Kill Radec by destroying all Field Hospitals\n
-->  Eliminate remaining Freedom Guard\n
\s\s\s\s resistance
\2
The responsibility given you is great, but you continue to prove yourself worthy.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Imperium forces were unable to finish off the scattered Freedom Guard armies on Elmaean. The Freedom Guard's guerrilla forces used the dense jungle terrain to their advantage and routed the unwieldy Imperium armored divisions. The Imperium was repelled from the planet, and Freedom Guard commander Radec survived and was able to regroup his beleaguered forces.
\3
Your will is weak. Find resolution within yourself.



